<Project>
  <!-- Phase 1865 - every packable F# project ships its XML documentation file beside its DLL, so
       the `///` comments in its sources reach a consumer's hover and the package carries
       `lib/<tfm>/<Assembly>.xml`.

       WHY THIS IS NOT IN Directory.Build.props. That file is evaluated BEFORE the project body,
       and every project here declares `<IsPackable>` in its own project file, so the condition
       below would read an empty IsPackable there. The SDK reads GenerateDocumentationFile in
       Microsoft.NET.Sdk.BeforeCommon.targets, which is imported before any
       Directory.Build.targets, so that file is too late. `BeforeMicrosoftNETSdkTargets` is the
       SDK's seam between the two: imported after the project body and before the SDK decides.
       Directory.Build.props points it here.

       THE CONDITION is pack's own: a project packs unless it says `<IsPackable>false`, so test
       projects, samples, benchmarks and Build.fsproj are left exactly as they were. A project
       that sets GenerateDocumentationFile itself keeps its own value.

       F# ONLY, deliberately. F# reports no missing-documentation diagnostic, so the flip cannot
       break a build under TreatWarningsAsErrors. C# and Visual Basic do (CS1591 and its family),
       and the C# and VB packages are not yet documented to that standard; they are reported by
       the package-roster check (`tests/package-roster/PackageRoster.fs`) on every run rather
       than silently left out. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GenerateDocumentationFile)' == '' and '$(IsPackable)' != 'false' and '$(MSBuildProjectExtension)' == '.fsproj'">
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
